{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/HTTP-Triggered Azure Function.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/HTTP-Triggered Azure Function.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"http triggered azure function http triggered azure function","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/HTTP-Triggered Azure Function.md","fileName":"HTTP-Triggered Azure Function.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"HTTP-Triggered Azure Function","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-08 22:09\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Azure Logic Apps and Functions]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Azure Logic Apps and Functions","c8andnetcore30projectsusingazure.pdf","hands-onmobiledevelopmentwithnetcore.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/HTTP-Triggered Azure Function.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/HTTP-Triggered Azure Function.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"http triggered azure function http triggered azure function","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/HTTP-Triggered Azure Function.md","fileName":"HTTP-Triggered Azure Function.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"HTTP-Triggered Azure Function","heading":"HTTP-Triggered Azure Function","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"An HTTP-triggered Azure Function exposes a function through an HTTP request. Attributes identify the function name, accepted methods, route behavior, and authorization level, while the method receives the request and returns an HTTP action result.\n\nThe date-comparison function reads a JSON request body, performs its comparison, and returns a JSON-shaped flag. The HTTP boundary lets a Logic App call the function like another connected action without embedding the calculation in the workflow definition.\n\nIn the source, an HTTP trigger exposes focused C# computation through a managed endpoint, while other function triggers allow the same serverless model to react to queues, schedules, and service events without an always-running custom host.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Azure Logic Apps and Functions","c8andnetcore30projectsusingazure.pdf","hands-onmobiledevelopmentwithnetcore.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/HTTP-Triggered Azure Function.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/HTTP-Triggered Azure Function.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"http triggered azure function http triggered azure function","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/HTTP-Triggered Azure Function.md","fileName":"HTTP-Triggered Azure Function.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"HTTP-Triggered Azure Function","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[hands-onsoftwarearchitecturewithc8andnetcore3.pdf]]\n\n[[c8andnetcore30projectsusingazure.pdf]]\n\n[[hands-onmobiledevelopmentwithnetcore.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Azure Logic Apps and Functions","c8andnetcore30projectsusingazure.pdf","hands-onmobiledevelopmentwithnetcore.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}